From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegram-custom <telegram-custom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:26:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Media trust: media from untrusted chats waits for a tap

docs/trust.md Android v1. A chat is trusted when it is Saved Messages or
777000, marked by hand (people: 90-day grace, then by activity), a group you
created or a channel you run, or an active contact (3 days in 90 that they
wrote to you in private, logged on this device in tc_activity). Your own
non-forwarded messages always load; "Never trust" beats everything.

Untrusted, with tap to load on: no auto-download (DownloadController
funnels, story preload, rich messages, chat-list thumbnails), and one gate
in ImageReceiver.setImage for cells, the chat list and the pinned/reply bars
keeps only the embedded blurred thumbnail; animated and video stickers stay
still (dice and animated emoji excepted). The first tap on such a message
unlocks it for the session and rebinds the cell. Direct-URL web documents
never load while the model is on. Calls with untrusted users are relay-only.

Chat menu item with state-first labels, a once-per-chat toast "Media here
waits for a tap / Trust this chat", Settings -> Media trust (nine rows).
Rules are pure (TrustRules) and unit-tested by CI with plain javac.
